    </tei:note>
    <tei:note type="commentary" n="22" target="#note_22">
      <tei:p>Literally, “curtain.” The list of the seven names of the firmaments is found in multiple locations and multiple variations but the specific list on which this entire piyyuṭ is based, with Makhon before Ma’on, is found in Tanna d’Vei Eliyahu Zuta 9:1 and the minor Midrash on the Ten Commandments.</tei:p>
    </tei:note>
